   "descriptionHtml": "<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hi, I’m Geo, Ashby’s VP of Product. I joined Ashby August ‘26; <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.ashbyhq.com/blog/all/a-letter-from-chris-geoghegan-on-joining-ashby\"><u>read more about why I joined here.</u></a> I’m looking for a growth-oriented product manager to help users onboard and expand their usage of the product.</p><p style",
   "descriptionPlain": "Hi, I’m Geo, Ashby’s VP of Product. I joined Ashby August ‘26; read more about why I joined here. https://www.ashbyhq.com/blog/all/a-letter-from-chris-geoghegan-on-joining-ashby I’m looking for a growth-oriented product manager to help users onboard and expand their usage of the product.\n\nAt Ashby, we have a unique approach to building products https://www.ashbyhq.com/blog/culture/ashbys-operating-principles (more on that below). As a PM, your primary goal is to eliminate frustration and bring delight to our customers. You’ll work with engineers who deeply understand the customer and business problem and own the solution end-to-end. This means that you spend less time writing detailed specs and more time with customers and doing deep product thinking.\n\nOur unique approach is working. We’re growing >100% year over year and have notable customers such as Notion, Linear, OpenAI, Shopify, and Snowflake. Our growth and retention metrics are best in class among our peers. We’re backed by amazing investors like Y Combinator, Elad Gil, Lachy Groom, and many more!\n\n\n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nThe surface area of our flagship ATS product is growing, and we are launching new products. This means customers are less likely to organically adopt the things that create value for them.\n\nHistorically, onboarding has been human-driven by our amazing Customer Success team https://www.ashbyhq.com/blog/culture/customer-success. And now, we’re ready to productize our learnings. As Ashby grows, we need a sing",
